{
  "article": "Princess Märtha Louise of Norway, the visionary offspring of King Harald who has ruled Europe for many years, tied the knot with Californian self-professed sixth-generation shaman Durek Verrett in an unconventional ceremony on Saturday. Despite the non-traditional nature of their marriage, numerous onlookers gathered along the gloomy pathways of Geiranger in hopes of glimpsing the bride. At 52, Princess Märtha Louise, the sole daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja and currently fourth in line for the throne, was wed to 49-year-old Verrett. The event took place in Geiranger's four-star Hotel Union, within a typical Church of Norway setting, drawing both royalty and famed personalities. Accompanying the princess were her seven bridesmaids, which included her daughters, teenagers Leah and Emma Behn, from her previous marriage to the departed Norwegian writer Ari Behn whom she divorced in 2017. The celebration saw around 350 guests including her brother Crown Prince Haakon and Crown Princess Mette-Marit, Crown Princess Victoria of Sweden and her spouse Prince Daniel, along with Prince Constantijn and Princess Laurentien of the Netherlands. Known for leading a less typical royal existence, Princess Märtha Louise has claimed to possess clairvoyance and previously operated a school devoted to spiritual healing and angelic communication. In 2022, she announced her decision to resign from official royal responsibilities to better concentrate on her joint ventures with Verrett, aiming for a clearer separation from the royal family of Norway. Verrett, who presents himself as a 'servant of God' and 'energy activator' on social media, lists celebrities like Gwyneth Paltrow of Goop, whom he regards as a 'soul sister', among his clients."
}
```

